WEST LAFAYETTE FIRE DEPARTMENT
3OO NORTH STREETWEST LAFAYETTE, INDIANA 47906765.775.5L75Ensuring West Lolayette is olwoys a sole ond greot ploce to work, live, ond ploy.
Firefighter Clayton Zak attended a Fire lnspector I course provided by lndiana Homeland Security District 4.Firefighter Shane Chapman and Captain Eric Lamb participated in a rope anchoring class at Advanced RescueSolutions in Greenwood, lndia na
A total of 990 hours was spent on training this month by fire department members
Presented by Captain Grant Birge
WEST LAFAYETTE FIRE DEPARTMENT | 300 North Street I West Lafayette, lN 47906 |
westlafayette.i n.gov/f ire
ln September, we had our second joint fire training of the year with the Lafayette Fire Department. The WestLafayette Fire Department conducted this training. We also included the Purdue Universlty Fire Department and theWabash Township Fire Department. The training took place over three days and included all shifts. There were threedifferent training groups each day. lnstructors from all four departments assisted with the training. We also includedanother round of vehicle extrication on three cars donated to us by Subaru of lndiana Automotive.Our Captains continued with their Certified Public Manager course at BallState in Fishers, lndiana.Firefighter Tiffany zavitsky attended a two-day course in West Chester, Pennsylvania, which was Mayday and Rapidlntervention Team responsibility. The course focused on self-rescue situations and Rapid lntervention TeamResponse.

